<article class="env-lemma" id="039G">
       
      
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/039G">Lemma <span data-tag="039G">41.3.2</span>.</a> Let $A \to B$ be of finite type with $A$ a Noetherian ring. Let $\mathfrak q$ be a prime of $B$ lying over $\mathfrak p \subset A$. Then $A \to B$ is unramified at $\mathfrak q$ if and only if $A_{\mathfrak p} \to B_{\mathfrak q}$ is an unramified homomorphism of local rings. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
